<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ROT_WARM_MAT_1 — M3's third piece, the heat gene, shipped at v1 FALLBACK
    STRENGTH exactly as the spec's v1/v2 boundary requires: a plain
    ComfyTemperatureMin statOffset on vanilla Gene_ machinery, no new C#.
    The heat-PUSHING gene body (a carrier warming the room around them) is
    v2 polish and is deliberately not built here.

    DESIGN SOURCE, measured not guessed. design/Jawa/worldbuilding/
    genepack_mods_plunder.md (2026-09-06): neither genepack mod ships a
    GeneDef at all, and the closest existing numbers are two hediffs —
    `IgniFurnace` ("stomach furnace": ComfyTempMin -8, eats more, rests less)
    and `IgniWarm` (comfy band shifted down). This gene is that effect made
    heritable and stronger, with the same shape of cost:

      -20 ComfyTemperatureMin   = 2.5x IgniFurnace's -8, per the ticket's
                                  ruled number, and 2x vanilla Furskin's -10
                                  (MEASURED this pass: Furskin is
                                  biostatCpx 1 / biostatMet -1 at -10).
      biostatCpx 2 / met -3     = twice Furskin's complexity for twice its
                                  effect, and a metabolism cost past the
                                  linear scaling because this body is
                                  BURNING food for the heat — that is
                                  IgniFurnace's "eats more" carried over.
                                  In Biotech, negative metabolism IS the
                                  hunger-rate cost; no extra field needed.

    Biotech-only by MayRequire on the def: GeneDef content is inert without
    it (precedent: src/RimMandrake/GelatinousSlime/Defs/GeneDefs/
    SlimeGenes.xml). Ban 5 compliant: locally-beneficial genepack content,
    nothing to do with gene extraction or the Slime's reactor.

    ART OWED: iconPath reuses a vanilla gene icon.

    OWED / UNMEASURED: the ticket asks for it to ship "in Rot genepack loot
    only". Vanilla genepack generation draws from all eligible GeneDefs and
    has no biome-scoped source; restricting it would need a custom
    ThingSetMaker, which is not in this ticket's scope. Shipped as ordinary
    genepack-eligible content and flagged rather than faked.
  -->

  <GeneDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">
    <defName>RUT_Gene_Furnaceblood</defName>
    <label>furnaceblood</label>
    <labelShortAdj>furnacebled</labelShortAdj>
    <description>Carriers run a second metabolism in the gut wall — a slow fungal-style burn that does nothing useful except make heat, constantly. They steam faintly in cold air, sleep uncovered on nights that would kill a colonist, and eat like two people to pay for it.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Furskin</iconPath>
    <displayCategory>ResistanceAndWeakness</displayCategory>
    <displayOrderInCategory>90</displayOrderInCategory>
    <customEffectDescriptions>
      <li>Body runs hot at all times, at a constant food cost</li>
    </customEffectDescriptions>
    <biostatCpx>2</biostatCpx>
    <biostatMet>-3</biostatMet>
    <statOffsets>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-20</ComfyTemperatureMin>
    </statOffsets>
    <symbolPack>
      <prefixSymbols>
        <li>
          <symbol>ember</symbol>
        </li>
        <li>
          <symbol>kiln</symbol>
        </li>
      </prefixSymbols>
    </symbolPack>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
